javascript-
------------------
   ->Javascript is the scripting language as well as programming language.

Why we need JS?
---------------------

->To build the dynamic web application.
->to add functionality to the web applications.
->to manipulate HTML and CSS.
->To achieve DOM(Document object model) functionalities.
->To fetch data from server(API) and also to send data to server Js is required.

Difference between Java and Javascript:
----------------------------------------

  JAVA                                                         Javascript
  1.java is a object oriented programming language.            1. it is a scripting language as well as object based programming language.
  2.in java both compiler and interpreter will be present.     2.in js only interpreter will be there.
  3.java will support multi-threadding.                        3.js will support single call stack.
  4.java is a imperative in nature.                            4.js is a dynamically typed programming language(in js no need to definedata types to the variable).
  5.java is strictly typed.(follows syntax)                    5.weakly typed.
  6.supports interface                                         6.does not support interface.


  Tokens:
  ----------------

    ->Tokens are the smallest units/elements inthe JS program.

    CLASSIFICATIONS:
    ----------------
         1.Identifiers:
              ->Identifiers are the names given to the code.
                ex:-variable names, class names and function names.
              ->In the place of identifiers we cant use keywords.
         2.Literals:
            ->Literals are the values given to js code
              TYPES:
               1.String Literals
               2.Numeric Literals
         3.Keywords:
            -> these are the pre-defined words which has its own meaning.
            -> in JS total 66 keywords are there.
               ex:-int ,char, function, float, boolean, class, const, var, let, if,else, for, while, do, continue, switch, break, default, double, return, export, exports, finally, try, catch, super, this, throw, package, public, void, null, import, get, set, abstract, assert, byte, constant, enum, extends, delete, implements
               ..etc
         4.Seperators:
            ->Seperators are used to seperate the given code.
              ex:-[],{},(),''," ",.,,,etc
         5.Operators:
            ->Operators are used to perform operations on operands
              ex:-10+20

              TYPES:
                1.Assignment Operators(=,+=,-=,*=,/=)
                2.Relational operators(>,>=,<,<=,)
                3.Arithemetic operators(+,-,*,/,%,**)
                4.bitwise operators(&,|,^)
                5.Logic operators(&&,||,!)
                6.Unary operators(++,--)
                7Ternary operators(Condition? expr1 : expr2)
                8.shift operators(<<,>>)
                9.comparision operators(==,===,!=)

         6.Comments:
            ->Comments are used to comment the given code.
              TYPES:
                1.Single line-//
                2.Multi line-/*



DataTypes in JS:
------------------
    ->DataTypes represents the what type of data we storing on variables.
      TYPES:
        1.Primitive datatypes(immutable):
           1.Number
           2.String
           3.Boolean
           4.null
           5.undefine
           6.symbol
           7.bigInt
        2.Non-primitive datatypes(mutable, object de-referencing):
           1.Arrays
           2.Objects
           3.Functions
           .classtypes


Variables:
---------------
    ->Variables are named memory location used to data/values and it can change N number of times during execution

      str="javascript"
      str=10


      1.variable declaration
      2.variable initialization
      3.variable utilization
      4.variable re-initialization
      5.variable re-declaration

1.let
    ->let variables act as a local scope / block scope
    ->variable declaration and initialisation is possible in same / different line
    ->re- initialisation is possible but not re declaration
    ->we cant hoist the let variables

2.var
    ->var variables acts like a global scop(because var present in windows objectively)
    ->variable re-declaration and initialization is same/different line is possible
    ->we can hoist the var variable
    ->variable declaration and initialisation is possible in same / different line

3.const
    ->const variables acts like a global final(because once initialisation we cant modify data/values)
    ->variable re-declaration and initialization is same line is not possible 
    ->we cant hoist the var variable
    ->variable declaration and initialisation is possible in same  line but not in different line




    Hoisting:
    ------------
      ->Utilizing the variables before declaration.
      ->Hoisting is possible only through 'var' variable.

